, -0.00959014892578125, -0.08135986328125, 0.01398468017578125, -0.003566741943359375, -0.030120849609375, -0.049041748046875, 0.064208984375, -0.043182373046875, 0.036346435546875, -0.040618896484375, 0.0018053054809570312, -0.04052734375, -0.064208984375, -0.0079193115234375, 0.044342041015625, -0.057952880859375, 0.022857666015625, -0.0364990234375, -0.06683349609375, -0.032440185546875, 0.017242431640625, 0.045135498046875, -0.032257080078125, 0.004291534423828125, -0.0841064453125, -0.0546875, -0.042572021484375, 0.0022029876708984375, -0.00226593017578125, -0.005558013916015625, 0.00806427001953125, 0.044464111328125, 0.01448822021484375, -0.041015625, -0.033935546875, -0.00076961517333984375, 0.041015625, -0.0423583984375, 0.009185791015625, 0.0419921875, 0.0736083984375, 0.0028705596923828125, 0.06854248046875, 0.095947265625, 0.015838623046875, -0.028717041015625, 0.00689697265625, 0.0286102294921875, 0.02215576171875, -0.0078887939453125, -0.0296630859375, -0.0291748046875, -0.02471923828125, 0.034210205078125, -0.015411376953125, 0.0307769775390625, -0.017303466796875, -0.0245361328125, -0.01544189453125, 0.01305389404296875, -0.0531005859375, 0.00948333740234375, 0.00737762451171875, 0.005950927734375, 0.0027179718017578125, -0.01546478271484375, 0.0280914306640625, 0.0139312744140625, 0.0133056640625, 0.0029659271240234375, -0.003307342529296875, -0.0131378173828125, 0.0254669189453125, 0.0280914306640625, 0.05181884765625, 0.011627197265625, -0.01116943359375, -0.043121337890625, -0.025390625, -0.01433563232421875, -0.02349853515625, -0.05157470703125, -0.05511474609375, -0.0426025390625, -0.00736236572265625, -0.017974853515625, -0.0192718505859375, -0.02679443359375, -0.0214385986328125, -0.001739501953125, -0.057342529296875, 0.082275390625, -0.01425933837890625, 0.006694793701171875, 0.0115203857421875, 0.01116943359375, -0.0156707763671875, -0.039031982421875, 0.0294189453125, -0.032257080078125, -0.0127105712890625, -0.036773681640625, -0.02496337890625, 0.042205810546875, -0.011688232421875, 0.04693603515625, 0.0014591217041015625, 0.03594970703125, -0.01788330078125, -0.047210693359375, 0.0024394989013671875, 0.01448822021484375, 0.0302581787109375, -0.0153350830078125, -0.049774169921875, -0.02203369140625, -0.01218414306640625, -0.0029544830322265625, 0.036224365234375, -0.0439453125, 0.005767822265625, 0.01064300537109375, -0.0015125274658203125, -0.0195159912109375, -0.046295166015625, 0.074951171875, -0.01284027099609375, -0.0106964111328125, -0.051513671875, -0.055145263671875, 0.00942230224609375, -0.0216827392578125, -0.0269622802734375, -0.00681304931640625, -0.033599853515625, -0.0066375732421875, -0.0076904296875, -0.0028133392333984375, -0.004268646240234375, 0.0411376953125, 0.0127410888671875, -0.035186767578125, 0.049102783203125, -0.0129547119140625, 0.024627685546875, -0.0119781494140625, -0.02569580078125, 0.0158538818359375, 0.004589080810546875, 0.052947998046875, 0.09954833984375, 0.00997161865234375, 0.056304931640625, 0.00835418701171875, 0.005855560302734375, -0.0156707763671875, -0.0299530029296875, -0.048431396484375, -0.052734375, -0.007640838623046875], `id`: "52ff5c71-ffee-4a01-9bfe-4df437c96476", `document_type`: "document", `source_document_id`: 1, `text`: "Once we find similar vectors, we can query the corresponding text and send everything to an LLM to answer the question based on the context.\r\n\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n* The original data is embedded\r\n* User’s question is embedded\r\n* We find similar vectors to the question\r\n* Based on the vector we have the original text as well\r\n* We send everything to an LLM\r\n\r\n\r\nGiven the above examples, the resulting prompt to the LLM would look like this:\r\n\r\n\r\nBased on the given context, answer the question.\r\n\r\n\r\nContext:\r\nGoogle Drive integration is an important feature of Horizontal\r\nHorizontal has Jira integration\r\n\r\n\r\nQuestion\r\nwhat integrations does Horizontal have?\r\n\r\n\r\nIt’s quite powerful because it finds context based on the semantic meaning of words instead of a simple full-text search.\r\nGraphRAG\r\nTraditional RAG is great but it doesn’t take the relationships into account. It doesn’t care about how one piece of content is related to another. It only looks for semantically similar words.\r\n\r\n\r\nGraphRAG combines:\r\n* Graph traversal algorithms\r\n* And RAG\r\n\r\n\r\nIn a nutshell:\r\n* We store vector embeddings in the knowledge graph itself\r\n* We find a pivot node based on vector embeddings\r\n* We traverse the graph to find related information\r\n* We give context to an LLM and generate an answer\r\n\r\n\r\nHorizontal’s GraphRAG is implemented in the API, inside SearchEngine.\r\n\r\n\r\nIt uses community detection (later on that) for pivot node retrieval and BFS (breadth-first search) for relevance expansion.\r\n\r\n\r\nAgentic GraphRAG is the next evolution of this kind of search. There’s a basic implementation in the graph builder project. We’ll probably use some elements of it in the future.\r\n\r\n\r\nGraphRAG was invented by Microsoft in 2024. The name refers to the technique and their original library as well. Google search already incorporated it.\r\nCommunity detection\r\nA very important aspect of graphs and GraphRAG is community detection.\r\n\r\n\r\nThere are algorithms such as Louvain and Leiden detection that find related nodes in a graph and put them under the same community node.\r\n\r\n\r\nResulting in a structure like this: \r\n  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThese nodes come from documents that discuss possible marketing strategies for Horizontal. Purple nodes are communities. Each community has multiple nodes and they are related.\r\n\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n* Community: “Workflow software example”\r\n   * Node: “Calendly\r\n   * Node: “Scheduling meetings”\r\n* This part of the document talks about how different SaaS apps pick and solve different workflows inside a company. For example, Calendly, picked a very small workflow of scheduling meetings.\r\n\r\n\r\nGraphRAG and communities\r\nCommunity detection plays an important role in GraphRAG.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen the user asks a question, we try to find the best community nodes for the question. Based on embeddings.\r\n\r\n\r\nEach community has a text column with a summary and embedding. This describes what the community is about.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen finding a pivot, it’s actually a community node.\r\n\r\n\r\nFor example, if you ask a question about marketing strategies or customer acquisition, it will probably locate these communities:\r\n  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n________________\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is an excellent strategy when the question is about a “broad” topic that relies on relationships, for example:\r\n* What are the most important marketing strategies?\r\n* What is the main positioning of the product?\r\n* Why did we develop “Feature XYZ” in a certain way?\r\n\r\n\r\nThese questions are answered in multiple Google Docs, Slack threads, hundreds of graph nodes, dozens of community nodes, etc. Finding a pivot node, and doing relevance expansion can result in great answers.\r\n\r\n\r\nBut when the question is something like:\r\n* What did I discuss with Peter?\r\n* Who is responsible for feature XYZ?\r\n* Give me our logo file\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen the question is more specific this technique will not work very well. For example, “What did I discuss with Peter?” there’s a really good chance that the name “Peter” cannot be found in any community node.", `_node_content`: "{\"id_\": \"52ff5c71-ffee-4a01-9bfe-4df437c96476\", \"embedding\": null, \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/1. Search engine overview\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 1, \"source_document_id\": 1, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\": [\"source_url\", \"document_chunk_id\", \"source_document_id\", \"document_type\"], \"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\": [\"source_type\", \"source_url\", \"document_chunk_id\", \"source_document_id\", \"document_type\"], \"relationships\": {\"1\": {\"node_id\": \"d515d623-1842-494c-b35d-82f8c7fbe2c9\", \"node_type\": \"4\", \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/1. Search engine overview\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 1, \"source_document_id\": 1, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"hash\": \"cb5e3058eb63b09d962b7b345c80edaa15e48612c9bbd638181837ed2e068e65\", \"class_name\": \"RelatedNodeInfo\"}, \"2\": {\"node_id\": \"112a565a-320e-4fa8-9273-dc750b718ddb\", \"node_type\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/1. Search engine overview\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 1, \"source_document_id\": 1, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"hash\": \"180c7a68f309fb8e81e980b7e91779aac20425f47c7af1d9c64474c35c2dc040\", \"class_name\": \"RelatedNodeInfo\"}}, \"metadata_template\": \"{key}: {value}\", \"metadata_separator\": \"\\n\", \"text\": \"\", \"mimetype\": \"text/plain\", \"start_char_idx\": 3777, \"end_char_idx\": 7769, \"metadata_seperator\": \"\\n\", \"text_template\": \"{metadata_str}\\n\\n{content}\", \"class_name\": \"TextNode\"}", `_node_type`: "TextNode", `doc_id`: "d515d623-1842-494c-b35d-82f8c7fbe2c9", `document_chunk_id`: 1, `document_id`: "d515d623-1842-494c-b35d-82f8c7fbe2c9", `ref_doc_id`: "d515d623-1842-494c-b35d-82f8c7fbe2c9", `source_type`: "google_drive", `title`: "Onboarding/1. Search engine overview"});
