, -0.0712890625, -0.027923583984375, -0.0223236083984375, -0.03985595703125, 0.00212860107421875, 0.00345611572265625, 0.0308380126953125, 0.00208282470703125, 0.0229949951171875, -0.017059326171875, -0.039093017578125, -0.0242156982421875, -0.0041046142578125, 0.04180908203125, -0.01174163818359375, -0.0251312255859375, 0.0257415771484375, 0.0012121200561523438, -0.007389068603515625, 0.01551055908203125, -0.043853759765625, -0.010498046875, -0.01444244384765625, -0.04351806640625, -0.023681640625, -0.04150390625, 0.05975341796875, -0.0196075439453125, -0.0090789794921875, -0.015716552734375, -0.0504150390625, -0.023834228515625, -0.01033782958984375, -0.0141754150390625, 0.0038433074951171875, -0.03857421875, 0.0167388916015625, -0.027252197265625, 0.003940582275390625, -0.00954437255859375, 0.040557861328125, 0.0193634033203125, -0.044097900390625, 0.052978515625, -0.00963592529296875, -0.003238677978515625, -0.0251007080078125, -0.0614013671875, -0.02166748046875, -0.008575439453125, 0.02899169921875, 0.077880859375, 0.024139404296875, 0.005069732666015625, -0.00452423095703125, 0.03289794921875, -0.0374755859375, -0.052734375, -0.059356689453125, -0.039215087890625, -0.012908935546875], `id`: "94de835f-b3d0-4664-856b-8dbb24a3087a", `document_type`: "document", `source_document_id`: 5, `text`: "A parent folder such as Communication should contain shared functionality and classes (mostly DTOs, value objects) across communication-related integrations. For example, Message, Reply, Attachment. These concepts work the same in a Slack or Team integration as well.\r\n\r\n\r\nPrompt\r\nHere’s the prompt that you can run to get an overview:\r\n________________\r\n\r\n\r\nI need you to analyze this Laravel project and provide me with a comprehensive architectural overview. Please examine the codebase systematically and help me understand how everything fits together.\r\nPlease provide:\r\n1. Project Overview\r\n* What does this application appear to do? (based on models, routes, and business logic)\r\n* What Laravel version is being used?\r\n* What are the main features/modules based on the code structure?\r\n* Are there any notable packages or dependencies I should be aware of? (check composer.json)\r\n2. Core Architecture Analysis\r\nDomain Models & Database\r\n* List the main Eloquent models (app/Models) and their key relationships\r\n* Identify the most central/important models (those with the most relationships or that appear in many places)\r\n* Note any interesting model traits, scopes, or custom attributes\r\n* Check for any database migrations that reveal important business logic\r\nBusiness Logic Layer\r\n* Identify the main Service classes (if any) and what they handle\r\n* Find any Repository pattern implementations\r\n* Locate Jobs, Events, Listeners, and Observers that handle important business processes\r\n* Note any custom Form Requests with complex validation rules\r\nControllers & Routes\r\n* Map out the main controller groups and their responsibilities\r\n* Identify which controllers handle the core functionality\r\n* Note any API controllers vs web controllers separation\r\n* Find any route groups, middleware, or route model bindings that are important\r\n3. Key Entry Points\r\nAPI Endpoints (if applicable)\r\nList the 5-10 most important API endpoints I should test, including:\r\n* The endpoint URL and HTTP method\r\n* What it does\r\n* Required parameters/payload\r\n* Which controller method handles it\r\n* Any authentication requirements\r\nConsole Commands\r\nList any custom Artisan commands (app/Console/Commands) that are important for:\r\n* Data processing\r\n* Scheduled tasks\r\n* Administrative functions\r\n* Development/debugging\r\nInclude the command signature and a brief description of what each does.\r\n4. Authentication & Authorization\r\n* How is authentication handled? (Laravel Sanctum, Passport, JWT, etc.)\r\n* Are there roles and permissions? If so, what system is used?\r\n* What are the main user types/roles?\r\n* Which middleware protects the routes?\r\n5. Data Flow Diagram\r\nCreate a simple text-based diagram showing how data flows through the main components. For example:\r\nUser Request → Route → Middleware → Controller → Service → Repository → Model → Database\r\n                                          ↓\r\n                                    Event/Job → Queue Worker\r\n6. Code Organization Patterns\r\n* What design patterns are consistently used? (Repository, Service, Action, etc.)\r\n* Are there any custom abstractions or base classes I should understand?\r\n* How is the code organized? (by feature, by layer, etc.)\r\n7. Testing & Development\r\n* What\'s the test coverage situation? (check tests/ directory)\r\n* Are there factories and seeders I can use to populate test data?\r\n* Any important environment variables in .env.example?\r\n8. Quick Start Recommendations\r\nBased on your analysis, suggest:\r\n1. The first 3-5 files I should read to understand the core domain\r\n2. A sequence of API calls or commands I could run to see the main flow in action\r\n3. Which part of the codebase I should explore first to be productive quickly\r\n9. Potential Concerns or Code Smells\r\nNote any architectural concerns, deprecated patterns, or areas that might need refactoring (be constructive and brief).\r\nPlease use actual file paths, class names, and method names from the codebase in your response.", `_node_content`: "{\"id_\": \"94de835f-b3d0-4664-856b-8dbb24a3087a\", \"embedding\": null, \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 6, \"source_document_id\": 5, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\": [\"source_url\", \"document_chunk_id\", \"source_document_id\", \"document_type\"], \"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\": [\"source_type\", \"source_url\", \"document_chunk_id\", \"source_document_id\", \"document_type\"], \"relationships\": {\"1\": {\"node_id\": \"7dbaed73-f176-485b-a0f2-ef187f489271\", \"node_type\": \"4\", \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 6, \"source_document_id\": 5, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"hash\": \"23ed1ce3c95a15e5d7a81452d828186d533e1f2dd96ae6ccb1fa9d207c3735d2\", \"class_name\": \"RelatedNodeInfo\"}, \"2\": {\"node_id\": \"2c55c068-706a-4b90-911f-1cc44e76328e\", \"node_type\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 6, \"source_document_id\": 5, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"hash\": \"45fe3fea7a646712f4c10eb06084261c8e1e92847843d64017d813fcbaa46142\", \"class_name\": \"RelatedNodeInfo\"}}, \"metadata_template\": \"{key}: {value}\", \"metadata_separator\": \"\\n\", \"text\": \"\", \"mimetype\": \"text/plain\", \"start_char_idx\": 3963, \"end_char_idx\": 7934, \"metadata_seperator\": \"\\n\", \"text_template\": \"{metadata_str}\\n\\n{content}\", \"class_name\": \"TextNode\"}", `_node_type`: "TextNode", `doc_id`: "7dbaed73-f176-485b-a0f2-ef187f489271", `document_chunk_id`: 6, `document_id`: "7dbaed73-f176-485b-a0f2-ef187f489271", `ref_doc_id`: "7dbaed73-f176-485b-a0f2-ef187f489271", `source_type`: "google_drive", `title`: "Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase"});
