28125, 0.032806396484375, -0.03350830078125, 0.054443359375, -0.00021851062774658203, 0.006282806396484375, -0.02972412109375, -0.0190582275390625, -0.003940582275390625, 0.041534423828125, 0.0299530029296875, -0.024505615234375, -0.0265350341796875, 0.006610870361328125, 0.03564453125, -0.0162811279296875, 0.040985107421875, -0.050201416015625, 0.005245208740234375, -0.00848388671875, -0.00820159912109375, 0.004283905029296875, -0.007144927978515625, 0.0230255126953125, -0.00556182861328125, 0.02899169921875, -0.0041351318359375, -0.030364990234375, -0.03302001953125, -0.021636962890625, -0.09063720703125, -0.0150604248046875, -0.06195068359375, 0.0276947021484375, 0.031097412109375, 0.0199432373046875, 0.00061893463134765625, 0.0648193359375, 0.017303466796875, 0.003795623779296875, 0.024749755859375, -0.007144927978515625, -0.031524658203125, -0.037261962890625, -0.0177154541015625, 0.0192718505859375, 0.02276611328125, -0.000484466552734375, 0.0816650390625, 0.061370849609375, 0.03851318359375, 0.006832122802734375, 0.0259246826171875, 0.055908203125, -0.0071563720703125, -0.06048583984375, -0.056488037109375, 0.0343017578125], `id`: 64, `name`: "AWS VPC and Lambda-Database Connectivity", `summary`: "This community revolves around configuring AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) to enable secure connectivity between Lambda functions and private RDS databases. Key components include VPC setup with CIDR notation, subnets across multiple availability zones (AZs), internet gateways, route tables, and security groups. The primary relationship is the network configuration that allows Lambda functions (public by default) to access private databases by placing them within the same VPC. Distinctive characteristics include the detailed AWS resource configurations (like AWS::EC2::RouteTable and AWS::EC2::Subnet) and the focus on solving the connectivity challenge between serverless functions and private database resources."});
