815673828125, -0.0230865478515625, 0.039031982421875, 0.005817413330078125, -0.021209716796875, -0.031402587890625, -0.046600341796875, -0.0015058517456054688, 0.0242767333984375, 0.04302978515625, -0.023681640625, -0.035736083984375, 0.009185791015625, 0.0148162841796875, -0.02130126953125, 0.041900634765625, -0.03741455078125, -0.0023708343505859375, -0.031402587890625, -0.006488800048828125, -0.0092620849609375, 0.0032501220703125, 0.0193939208984375, 0.0112457275390625, 0.020538330078125, -0.013580322265625, -0.0300750732421875, -0.038177490234375, -0.018798828125, -0.0743408203125, -0.0107574462890625, -0.07952880859375, 0.03680419921875, 0.025390625, 0.01062774658203125, 0.015777587890625, 0.059356689453125, -0.004302978515625, -0.013092041015625, 0.0164947509765625, -0.00829315185546875, -0.0291748046875, -0.03985595703125, 0.009857177734375, -0.00084686279296875, 0.0152435302734375, -0.0028972625732421875, 0.06756591796875, 0.0650634765625, 0.0265045166015625, 0.00276947021484375, -0.01079559326171875, 0.055023193359375, 0.00249481201171875, -0.07708740234375, -0.0587158203125, 0.0350341796875], `id`: 62, `name`: "AWS RDS Database Security and Networking", `summary`: "This community revolves around AWS RDS databases being private by default for security reasons, and the networking challenges this creates when integrating with public-facing Lambda functions. The core issue is that Lambdas cannot access private RDS databases, requiring solutions like VPCs (Virtual Private Clouds) to create secure, isolated networks. Key components include internet gateways, subnets spread across availability zones, and route tables to manage traffic between these elements. The grouping serves to address the technical challenge of securely connecting public serverless functions with private database resources in AWS. What makes this distinct is its focus on AWS-specific networking configurations to solve a common cloud architecture problem."});
