29697418212890625, 2.1815299987792969e-05, -0.03448486328125, -0.01161956787109375, -0.00010854005813598633, -0.047271728515625, 0.01444244384765625, -0.06939697265625, 0.004730224609375, -0.0275115966796875, -0.06158447265625, -0.0280609130859375, 0.0162353515625, 0.0509033203125, -0.038116455078125, -0.05810546875, -0.00316619873046875, 0.046539306640625, 0.0096282958984375, 0.050048828125, -0.0168914794921875, -0.01788330078125, 0.004222869873046875, 0.01546478271484375, -0.02166748046875, -0.048980712890625, 0.066650390625, -0.005214691162109375, 0.01261138916015625, -0.032257080078125, -0.0107421875, -0.058197021484375, -0.052703857421875, -0.0247955322265625, 0.00899505615234375, -0.04046630859375, 0.01081085205078125, -0.015716552734375, 0.015960693359375, -0.0290985107421875, 0.00885009765625, 0.01303863525390625, -0.0211029052734375, -0.0211181640625, -0.0184326171875, -0.0196380615234375, -0.0169830322265625, 0.037811279296875, 0.0024204254150390625, 0.0596923828125, 0.043975830078125, 0.07818603515625, 0.00864410400390625, 0.01000213623046875, -0.01276397705078125, -0.0108489990234375, -0.055694580078125, -0.0460205078125, -0.05224609375, -0.0426025390625, -0.0305938720703125], `id`: 13, `name`: "Code Duplication Management Strategies", `summary`: "This community revolves around the challenges and strategies for handling code duplication in software development. It emphasizes the balance between innovation and consistency, advocating for pragmatic approaches like waiting for multiple occurrences before creating abstractions. Key relationships include the tension between immediate refactoring (creating new functions) versus premature abstraction (interfaces/design patterns). The concepts serve to guide developers in making informed decisions about when and how to address duplicated code segments, particularly 10-line sections across classes. Distinctively, it challenges conventional wisdom by suggesting that sometimes leaving duplication temporarily can lead to better long-term architectural decisions."});
