-0.038970947265625, -0.0144805908203125, -0.036895751953125, -0.04608154296875, 0.01442718505859375, -0.048828125, -0.004116058349609375, -0.00775909423828125, -0.05126953125, -0.04833984375, 0.032318115234375, 0.040435791015625, -0.03857421875, -0.0701904296875, -0.00247955322265625, 0.032196044921875, -0.0172882080078125, 0.0374755859375, -0.049468994140625, 0.004756927490234375, -0.004352569580078125, -0.0182342529296875, -0.0308074951171875, -0.032501220703125, 0.05511474609375, -0.0239105224609375, 0.034576416015625, -0.01108551025390625, -0.00713348388671875, -0.07000732421875, -0.06915283203125, 0.016204833984375, 0.024261474609375, 0.000179290771484375, -0.0117340087890625, -0.04010009765625, -0.01140594482421875, -0.0333251953125, 0.0242767333984375, 0.0237579345703125, -0.05389404296875, -0.001132965087890625, -0.0307159423828125, -0.062469482421875, -0.01361846923828125, 0.02691650390625, 0.026702880859375, 0.0212554931640625, 0.0682373046875, 0.11669921875, 0.03497314453125, 0.01282501220703125, -0.019927978515625, 0.0186004638671875, -0.07098388671875, -0.04925537109375, -0.02288818359375, -0.051361083984375, 0.0020580291748046875], `id`: 5, `name`: "Innovation vs. Consistency in Coding", `summary`: "This community explores the tension between maintaining consistency and embracing innovation in software development. It highlights how blindly following existing patterns (like code duplication rules) can lead to poor decisions, advocating instead for informed decision-making based on accumulated information. Key relationships show that more information leads to better decisions, particularly when deciding whether to abstract or duplicate code. The concepts serve to guide developers in making pragmatic choices about when to innovate versus when to maintain consistency. What makes this distinct is its focus on real-world coding dilemmas and practical heuristics for decision-making."});
