 -0.059326171875, 0.037353515625, -0.0230560302734375, -0.037322998046875, -0.03704833984375, 0.058349609375, -0.03759765625, 0.04107666015625, -0.01151275634765625, 0.02630615234375, -0.0048980712890625, -0.0352783203125, -0.0290985107421875, 0.09710693359375, -0.037933349609375, 0.0321044921875, 0.0037479400634765625, -0.07830810546875, -0.05218505859375, 0.00963592529296875, 0.0311431884765625, -0.031524658203125, 0.0031833648681640625, -0.0989990234375, -0.046295166015625, -0.052978515625, 0.005184173583984375, -0.0182952880859375, 0.0011005401611328125, 0.0013027191162109375, 0.04205322265625, 0.0263671875, -0.0246124267578125, -0.02471923828125, 0.01538848876953125, 0.037933349609375, -0.053985595703125, 0.00097036361694335938, 0.047027587890625, 0.1036376953125, -0.0426025390625, 0.0260162353515625, 0.081298828125, 0.0306396484375, -0.0352783203125, 0.0015411376953125, 0.02496337890625, 0.03436279296875, -0.038116455078125, -0.07598876953125, -0.061309814453125, -0.01506805419921875, 0.00649261474609375, 0.01702880859375, 0.00085926055908203125, -0.008148193359375, 0.01425933837890625, -0.01264190673828125, 0.0174102783203125, -0.07720947265625, 0.0014905929565429688, -0.01290130615234375, 0.0277099609375, 0.01018524169921875, -0.031951904296875, 0.0263214111328125, 0.04193115234375, 0.037933349609375, 0.0180511474609375, -0.0012693405151367188, -0.0291748046875, 0.025390625, 0.00980377197265625, 0.01486968994140625, -0.031341552734375, -0.0190887451171875, -0.06256103515625, -0.03546142578125, -0.04034423828125, -0.037567138671875, -0.07061767578125, -0.0614013671875, -0.038726806640625, -0.0032444000244140625, -0.04833984375, -0.0301513671875, 0.0066375732421875, 1.6033649444580078e-05, -0.0309906005859375, -0.034149169921875, 0.060821533203125, -0.01090240478515625, -0.0079345703125, 0.0225677490234375, 0.03790283203125, -0.056549072265625, -0.03277587890625, 0.01629638671875, -0.00707244873046875, -0.034637451171875, -0.01375579833984375, -0.038238525390625, 0.0028362274169921875, 0.00653076171875, 0.039306640625, -0.032073974609375, 0.039459228515625, -0.031768798828125, -0.04132080078125, -0.0082550048828125, -0.00655364990234375, 0.0278778076171875, -0.00794219970703125, -0.07330322265625, 0.020660400390625, 0.002605438232421875, 0.0057525634765625, 0.028533935546875, -0.0560302734375, 0.03302001953125, 0.0087738037109375, -0.059173583984375, -0.004978179931640625, -0.0268402099609375, 0.054443359375, -0.02618408203125, -0.01264190673828125, -0.027130126953125, -0.0692138671875, -0.046722412109375, -0.022796630859375, -0.00455474853515625, 0.02044677734375, -0.02734375, 0.01451873779296875, -0.0081787109375, -0.00021374225616455078, -0.0256805419921875, 0.0161590576171875, 0.01568603515625, -0.0239105224609375, 0.06268310546875, -0.028167724609375, 0.012603759765625, -0.003940582275390625, -0.0546875, 0.016571044921875, 0.0090179443359375, 0.060821533203125, 0.07305908203125, 0.02728271484375, 0.00482940673828125, -0.0045013427734375, 0.027587890625, -0.04547119140625, -0.0306396484375, -0.061431884765625, -0.015167236328125, -0.0091094970703125], `id`: "8cdf6a93-1596-4af4-905b-13aa88f6dfa7", `document_type`: "document", `source_document_id`: 5, `text`: "title: Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase, body: ﻿Discovering the codebase\r\nhorizontal.app\r\nOverview\r\nCodebases change fast. There’s no point of documenting the structure of an early project that will change in a few weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\nInstead, you should use Claude Code or Cursor to do that.\r\n\r\n\r\nOpen Claude Code in the given project (such as api) and run /init\r\nThis will update CLAUDE.md\r\n\r\n\r\nThen run the following prompt at the end of this file.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis will give you an overview of the project. If you want to understand a specific part of the codebase use a similar prompt and tell it to analyze only the given area.\r\nImportant models\r\nThe most important model is Document\r\n\r\n\r\nEvery piece of information we index becomes a Document:\r\n* Drive files\r\n* Jira tickets\r\n* Slack conversations\r\n* Etc\r\n\r\n\r\nBut a Drive file (for example) can be very very long. In order to effectively process them we need to chunk them into manageable pieces. This is important because of memory usage, LLM context windows, etc.\r\n\r\n\r\nDocumentChunk stores these chunks.\r\n\r\n\r\nEach Document can have some “additional” information, for example:\r\n* A Drive file can have comments\r\n* It has revisions\r\n* A Jira ticket also has comments\r\n* Etc\r\n\r\n\r\nThese are stored in related tables such as DocumentComment.\r\n\r\n\r\nDocuments table\r\n* source_type refers to the 3rd party tool where the data comes from:\r\n   * google_drive\r\n   * jira\r\n   * slack\r\n   * github\r\n   * etc\r\n* source_id is the original ID of the document from the 3rd party API. Usually, each provider has an ID attached to a file, message, etc\r\n\r\n\r\nThese columns are important because we can identify the document when updating our own DB with new data coming from 3rd parties.\r\n\r\n\r\n* source_url is a URL where users can see the original document. For example, the Drive URL to the file when to document is a Drive file.\r\n\r\n\r\n* title is the “title” of a document. For example:\r\nSource\r\n\tTitle\r\n\tGoogle Drive\r\n\tFilename\r\n\tJira\r\n\tIssue title\r\n\tGitHub PR\r\n\tName of the PR\r\n\tSlack\r\n\tCustom\r\n\t\r\n\r\nThis is important because when a user searches something in Horizontal, we’ll show the sources that we’ve used to come up with an answer. Users will see these titles.\r\n\r\n\r\nSince Slack messages don’t have real “titles” we can come up with something like this: “John Doe’s message in #general”\r\n\r\n\r\nThis holds some useful context for the user.\r\n\r\n\r\n* metadata contains the entire object from the 3rd party API.\r\n* preview is the first sentence of the document. Not sure if it\'s needed in the long term.\r\n* priority is not used anymore\r\n* team_id is not used anymore\r\n\r\n\r\ndocument_chunks table \r\nEach document is split into smaller chunks. This is important because of document size. It’s hard to effectively process 5MB of text. Memory issues, LLM context windows, etc.\r\n\r\n\r\n* document_id is foreign key to documents\r\n* body is the chunk\r\n* position is the 1-indexed position of the current chunk in the document. If there are three chunks they go like 1,2,3\r\n* search_vector is created automatically\r\n\r\n\r\nChunking is done by the TextChunker class.\r\nIndexing\r\nIndexing refers to the process when we download data from 3rd party APIs and build our own databases.\r\n\r\n\r\nEverything is handled in the app/Jobs/Indexing namespace.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe plan is to have a namespace structure like this:\r\n* app/Jobs/Indexing\r\n   * app/Jobs/Indexing/TaskManagement\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/TaskManagement/Jira\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/TaskManagement/Linear\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/TaskManagement/ClickUp\r\n   * app/Jobs/Indexing/Communication\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/Communication/Slack\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/Communication/Teams\r\n   * app/Jobs/Indexing/Storage\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/Storage/GoogleDrive\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/Storage/Dropbox\r\n   * app/Jobs/Indexing/CodeRepository\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/Storage/GitHub\r\n      * app/Jobs/Indexing/Storage/GitLab\r\n\r\n\r\nA folder such as Slack should contain only Slack-related code.\r\nA parent folder such as Communication should contain shared functionality and classes (mostly DTOs, value objects) across communication-related integrations. For example, Message, Reply, Attachment. These concepts work the same in a Slack or Team integration as well.", `_node_content`: "{\"id_\": \"8cdf6a93-1596-4af4-905b-13aa88f6dfa7\", \"embedding\": null, \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 6, \"source_document_id\": 5, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\": [\"source_url\", \"document_chunk_id\", \"source_document_id\", \"document_type\"], \"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\": [\"source_type\", \"source_url\", \"document_chunk_id\", \"source_document_id\", \"document_type\"], \"relationships\": {\"1\": {\"node_id\": \"6bf2a344-5f24-410e-b41c-1d983d782a47\", \"node_type\": \"4\", \"metadata\": {\"title\": \"Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase\", \"source_type\": \"google_drive\", \"source_url\": null, \"document_chunk_id\": 6, \"source_document_id\": 5, \"document_type\": \"document\"}, \"hash\": \"23ed1ce3c95a15e5d7a81452d828186d533e1f2dd96ae6ccb1fa9d207c3735d2\", \"class_name\": \"RelatedNodeInfo\"}, \"3\": {\"node_id\": \"23a5f2f4-b8ac-4eb6-9ce3-5e49fdebf47f\", \"node_type\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {}, \"hash\": \"3ebe62fac3442d1a21cc58f27d0b180ecab8819df1f3c3f6253926686bb1ae10\", \"class_name\": \"RelatedNodeInfo\"}}, \"metadata_template\": \"{key}: {value}\", \"metadata_separator\": \"\\n\", \"text\": \"\", \"mimetype\": \"text/plain\", \"start_char_idx\": 0, \"end_char_idx\": 4230, \"metadata_seperator\": \"\\n\", \"text_template\": \"{metadata_str}\\n\\n{content}\", \"class_name\": \"TextNode\"}", `_node_type`: "TextNode", `doc_id`: "6bf2a344-5f24-410e-b41c-1d983d782a47", `document_chunk_id`: 6, `document_id`: "6bf2a344-5f24-410e-b41c-1d983d782a47", `ref_doc_id`: "6bf2a344-5f24-410e-b41c-1d983d782a47", `source_type`: "google_drive", `title`: "Onboarding/3. Discovering the codebase"});
